From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: allow camera EGL configuration reads

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_mainline_common
License: Apache-2.0 (modified upstream sources)
Base-commit: f49f55117276cc2603fd7f6aeb78b859535f8e8d

Libcamera initializes EGL for the software ISP's GPU debayer path. Mesa
reads vendor.mesa configuration, and GraphicsEnv initialization reads
ro.zygote.disable_gl_preload even outside a zygote process.

Allow those typed property reads without granting the much broader
default_prop access requested by optional legacy Mesa/minigbm probes.
Do not use gpu_access here: these missing property reads do not require
additional device-node or sysfs permissions.

--- a/sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te
@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@
 # vendor.camera.* configuration
 get_prop(hal_camera_default, vendor_camera_prop)
 
+# Mesa and GraphicsEnv configuration used by libcamera's EGL path.
+get_prop(hal_camera_default, vendor_mesa_prop)
+get_prop(hal_camera_default, zygote_config_prop)
+
 # Camera hotplug: list and watch /dev for video nodes
 allow hal_camera_default device:dir { r_dir_perms watch };
